The loop now walks raw pointers over the vector's storage instead of calling `size()` and `operator[]` on every iteration. It checks the same fields in the same order and returns the same pointer, so behavior is unchanged. Any speedup is likely small, because the per-field `GetNum()` call is still there.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* p = fields.data();
    Field* const end = p + fields.size();
    for (; p != end; ++p)
    {
        if (p->GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return p;
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```